hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17677","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us: Bakr ibn Sawadah narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Nu'aym, from Hibban ibn Buh al-Suda'i, companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: My people disbelieved, so I was told that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had equipped an army against them. I came to him and said: My people are upon Islam. He said: Is that so? I said: Yes. He said: I followed him through my night until morning. I called the adhan for prayer when morning came, and he gave me a vessel from which I performed ablution. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his fingers in the vessel and it burst forth as springs. He said: Whoever among you wishes to perform ablution, let him perform ablution. I performed ablution and prayed, and he put me in charge over them and gave me their charity. A man stood up to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: So-and-so wronged me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no good in leadership for a Muslim. Then a man came asking for charity, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Charity is a headache in the head and a burning in the belly, or a disease. I gave him my document, or the document of my command and my charity. He said: What is your affair? I said: How can I accept it when I heard from you what I heard? He said: It is as you heard."
